       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. The rationale you gave doesn't explain a dose of 1000 mg. Wanting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds isn't a clinical reason for five times the maximum dose. Entering it would put the patient at serious risk of harm, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac arrhythmia.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** Give me 50, 100, or 200 mg and I'll enter it immediately. If the aim is to have the patient's treatment settled before evening rounds, a therapeutic dose does that.\n- **Call pharmacy.** If you think there's an unusual clinical situation, a pharmacist or toxicology/psychiatry consult can review it with you. That route is also the right one if the order needs to go through a formal override process.\n- **Check the intent.** If you meant a different drug or a different unit, tell me and I'll re-enter it correctly.\n\nI'm happy to help with any of these."
      }
